This plugin will display a notification each time a package with type
"kdeconnect.telephony" is received. The type of notification will change
depending on the contents of the field "event" (string).

Valid contents for "event" are: "ringing", "talking", "missedCall" and "sms".
"sms" is ignored. "talking" replaces the ringing notification with a "call in
progress" one if the device supports call actions, otherwise it is ignored.

If the incoming package contains a "phoneNumber" string field, the notification
will also display it. Note that "phoneNumber" can be a contact name instead
of an actual phone number.

If the incoming package contains "isCancel" set to true, the call notification
is closed.

If the device supports "kdeconnect.telephony.request_action", the notifications
offer Answer / Reject / Hang up (also available over DBus and kdeconnect-cli),
and the device replies with "kdeconnect.telephony.action_status". Answering
with audio on this computer requests a "call" stream from the audiostream
plugin of the device. See docs/specs/callhandoff.md for the protocol.
